      "id": "854938245003a70d",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;Exclusive: Restoration work at Bath Assembly Rooms unearths Roman ditches containing pottery, coins and fragments of a military helmet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The restoration of a Georgian building in Bath once frequented by Jane Austen has unexpectedly provided a tantalising glimpse into the life of the city’s Roman suburbanites.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A network of Roman ditches containing pottery, coins, glassware and a fragment of a military helmet has been found beneath &lt;a href=\"https://www.nationaltrust.org.uk/visit/bath-bristol/bath-assembly-rooms\"&gt;Bath Assembly Rooms&lt;/a&gt; in the north of the city.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/sep/23/archaeologists-clues-suburban-life-roman-times-bath\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
