      "id": "0e6fadb5fa76b4b7",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;In today’s newsletter: The PM’s first face‑to‑face with​ the US president marks a fragile reset&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Good morning. In the early hours of Tuesday a plane carrying Andy Burnham, a handful of UK ministers, an excited group of British political journalists, and Burnham’s wife, Marie France, landed at a New York airport for one of Burnham’s first major outings as prime minister: a face-to-face meeting with Donald Trump.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Considering the president once described Burnham as the mayor of “a town,” and the prime minister once said Trump wouldn’t be welcome in said town (Manchester), the meeting yesterday afternoon went remarkably well.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UN general assembly &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Donald Trump has called on nations to unite to isolate Tehran and bring down global energy prices, as he gave a bellicose &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/trump-calls-on-allies-enforce-complete-economic-isolation-iran-un-speech\"&gt;defence of his administration’s foreign policy&lt;/a&gt; and decision to strike Iran.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The far right &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Charities &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/far-right-activist-daniel-thomas-slashes-dinghy-with-blade-while-rescue-worker-onboard\"&gt;have condemned footage&lt;/a&gt; of a far-right activist using a blade to slash an inflatable dinghy in the Channel while a rescue worker was onboard, in a further escalation of organised anti-immigration protest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK news &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Children as young as 13 in the UK have been referred to a specialist clinic for a “devastating” bladder condition &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/sep/22/liverpool-alder-hey-hospital-rise-children-ketamine-bladder-addiction\"&gt;linked to sustained use of ketamine&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;West Bank &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| British banks and financial institutions are &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/mps-uk-banks-investment-israeli-settlement-trade-ban\"&gt;receiving warnings from MPs&lt;/a&gt; that they should not invest in Israel’s E1 settlement project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UK politics &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;| Andy Burnham has opened the door to fighting the next election on the &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/22/andy-burnham-fails-rule-out-brexit-reversal-next-labour-manifesto\"&gt;UK rejoining the EU&lt;/a&gt;, but said his immediate priority was continuing to rebuild bridges with European allies.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/wednesday-briefing-can-burnham-seek-a-different-path-to-trumps-world-order\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
      "title": "Wednesday briefing: ​Can Burnham ​seek a ​different ​path​ to Trump’s world order?",
      "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/23/wednesday-briefing-can-burnham-seek-a-different-path-to-trumps-world-order",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-23T05:45:26.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "source": "The Guardian — World [T3]",
        "category": "news"
      }
    },
