      "id": "b9fd8215033869c9",
      "text": "&lt;p&gt;PM aims to ‘stem poisonous tide’ of disinformation and deepfakes with National Centre for Information Defence&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Security chiefs will set up a new national centre to tackle disinformation and deepfakes from hostile states such as Russia, Andy Burnham has announced, saying the government had a duty to “stem the poisonous tide” from damaging British interests.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The National Centre for Information Defence will “detect, attribute and disrupt” information attacks by foreign powers, many of which are enabled by &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/artificialintelligenceai\"&gt;AI&lt;/a&gt;, bringing together the intelligence agencies, law enforcement and social media companies.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/23/andy-burnham-national-centre-russian-disinformation-deepfakes\"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;",
